  ('IN', 'IN-S-12-INTER', 'Sale to another State — IGST 12 %', '{}'::jsonb, 'Seller and place of supply in different States: integrated tax, one posting', 'percent', 12, 'sale', 'domestic', date '2017-07-01', date '2025-09-21', 'Section 7 of the Integrated Goods and Services Tax Act: a supply where the location of the supplier and the place of supply are in two different States, two Union territories or a State and a Union territory is an inter-State supply, and section 5(1) of the same Act levies the integrated tax on it at the whole rate, collected by the Centre alone. `applies_when.supply_vs_seller: other` is section 7 in the vocabulary of the core: the place of supply lies outside the State of the seller''s registration. The rate: Schedule II of Notification No. 1/2017-Integrated Tax (Rate) and of the Central Tax (Rate) notification of the same number, 28 June 2017. Notification No. 9/2025 superseded both with effect from 22 September 2025 and carries no schedule at 12 %: the goods it held were moved to 5 % or to 18 %, which is why this code closes on 21 September 2025. It stays in the pack so that a supply invoiced before that day keeps its code. The taxable value goes to column 2 of line 3.1(a) of FORM GSTR-3B and the tax to its column 3.', 'S', null, 40, 'gst', true, '{}'::tax_condition[], null, false, false, null, 'igst-rate-9-2025', null, null, null, 'other'),
  ('IN', 'IN-S-12-INTRA', 'Sale within the State — GST 12 % (CGST 6 % + SGST/UTGST 6 %)', '{}'::jsonb, 'Seller and place of supply in the same State: central tax and State tax, half each', 'percent', 12, 'sale', 'domestic', date '2017-07-01', date '2025-09-21', 'Section 8 of the Integrated Goods and Services Tax Act: a supply where the location of the supplier and the place of supply are in the same State or the same Union territory is an intra-State supply, and on it section 9(1) of the Central Goods and Services Tax Act levies the central tax and the State Goods and Services Tax Act of that State (the Union Territory Goods and Services Tax Act, in a Union territory without a legislature) levies the State or Union territory tax, each at half the rate — the Central Tax (Rate) notification and each State''s own notification print the same schedules at half the integrated rate. One code carries the whole rate and its postings split it: half to the central tax account and to the Central Tax column of the line, half to the State/UT tax account and to the State/UT Tax column. `applies_when.supply_vs_seller: same` is section 8 in the vocabulary of the core: the place of supply lies in the State the seller is registered in, which is the State of its GSTIN, so the company''s own territory has to be set to that State. The rate: Schedule II of Notification No. 1/2017-Integrated Tax (Rate) and of the Central Tax (Rate) notification of the same number, 28 June 2017. Notification No. 9/2025 superseded both with effect from 22 September 2025 and carries no schedule at 12 %: the goods it held were moved to 5 % or to 18 %, which is why this code closes on 21 September 2025. It stays in the pack so that a supply invoiced before that day keeps its code. The taxable value goes to column 2 of line 3.1(a) of FORM GSTR-3B and the two halves of the tax to its columns 4 and 5.', 'S', null, 30, 'gst', true, '{}'::tax_condition[], null, false, false, null, 'igst-rate-9-2025', null, null, null, 'same'),
  ('IN', 'IN-S-18-INTER', 'Sale to another State — IGST 18 %', '{}'::jsonb, 'Seller and place of supply in different States: integrated tax, one posting', 'percent', 18, 'sale', 'domestic', date '2017-07-01', null, 'Section 7 of the Integrated Goods and Services Tax Act: a supply where the location of the supplier and the place of supply are in two different States, two Union territories or a State and a Union territory is an inter-State supply, and section 5(1) of the same Act levies the integrated tax on it at the whole rate, collected by the Centre alone. `applies_when.supply_vs_seller: other` is section 7 in the vocabulary of the core: the place of supply lies outside the State of the seller''s registration. The rate: Schedule II of Notification No. 9/2025-Integrated Tax (Rate) and of the Central Tax (Rate) notification of the same number, 17 September 2025, in force from 22 September 2025, whose entry 639 also makes 18 % the rate of any goods no other schedule names; the rate stood at 18 % under Schedule III of Notification No. 1/2017 as well. Most services are taxed at the same rate under Notification No. 11/2017-Central Tax (Rate). The taxable value goes to column 2 of line 3.1(a) of FORM GSTR-3B and the tax to its column 3.', 'S', null, 60, 'gst', true, '{}'::tax_condition[], null, false, false, null, 'igst-rate-9-2025', null, null, null, 'other'),
  ('IN', 'IN-S-18-INTRA', 'Sale within the State — GST 18 % (CGST 9 % + SGST/UTGST 9 %)', '{}'::jsonb, 'Seller and place of supply in the same State: central tax and State tax, half each', 'percent', 18, 'sale', 'domestic', date '2017-07-01', null, 'Section 8 of the Integrated Goods and Services Tax Act: a supply where the location of the supplier and the place of supply are in the same State or the same Union territory is an intra-State supply, and on it section 9(1) of the Central Goods and Services Tax Act levies the central tax and the State Goods and Services Tax Act of that State (the Union Territory Goods and Services Tax Act, in a Union territory without a legislature) levies the State or Union territory tax, each at half the rate — the Central Tax (Rate) notification and each State''s own notification print the same schedules at half the integrated rate. One code carries the whole rate and its postings split it: half to the central tax account and to the Central Tax column of the line, half to the State/UT tax account and to the State/UT Tax column. `applies_when.supply_vs_seller: same` is section 8 in the vocabulary of the core: the place of supply lies in the State the seller is registered in, which is the State of its GSTIN, so the company''s own territory has to be set to that State. The rate: Schedule II of Notification No. 9/2025-Integrated Tax (Rate) and of the Central Tax (Rate) notification of the same number, 17 September 2025, in force from 22 September 2025, whose entry 639 also makes 18 % the rate of any goods no other schedule names; the rate stood at 18 % under Schedule III of Notification No. 1/2017 as well. Most services are taxed at the same rate under Notification No. 11/2017-Central Tax (Rate). The taxable value goes to column 2 of line 3.1(a) of FORM GSTR-3B and the two halves of the tax to its columns 4 and 5.', 'S', null, 50, 'gst', true, '{}'::tax_condition[], null, false, false, null, 'igst-rate-9-2025', null, null, null, 'same'),
  ('IN', 'IN-S-28-INTER', 'Sale to another State — IGST 28 %', '{}'::jsonb, 'Seller and place of supply in different States: integrated tax, one posting', 'percent', 28, 'sale', 'domestic', date '2017-07-01', date '2026-01-31', 'Section 7 of the Integrated Goods and Services Tax Act: a supply where the location of the supplier and the place of supply are in two different States, two Union territories or a State and a Union territory is an inter-State supply, and section 5(1) of the same Act levies the integrated tax on it at the whole rate, collected by the Centre alone. `applies_when.supply_vs_seller: other` is section 7 in the vocabulary of the core: the place of supply lies outside the State of the seller''s registration. The rate: Schedule VII of Notification No. 9/2025-Integrated Tax (Rate), 17 September 2025, which kept 28 % for pan masala and tobacco products only (the 2017 notification had it as Schedule IV and reached far more goods). The Government moved those goods to 40 % and ended the compensation cess on them from 1 February 2026, when an additional excise duty and a Health and National Security Cess took the cess''s place, so this code closes on 31 January 2026. The taxable value goes to column 2 of line 3.1(a) of FORM GSTR-3B and the tax to its column 3.', 'S', null, 80, 'gst', true, '{}'::tax_condition[], null, false, false, null, 'igst-rate-9-2025', null, null, null, 'other'),
  ('IN', 'IN-S-28-INTRA', 'Sale within the State — GST 28 % (CGST 14 % + SGST/UTGST 14 %)', '{}'::jsonb, 'Seller and place of supply in the same State: central tax and State tax, half each', 'percent', 28, 'sale', 'domestic', date '2017-07-01', date '2026-01-31', 'Section 8 of the Integrated Goods and Services Tax Act: a supply where the location of the supplier and the place of supply are in the same State or the same Union territory is an intra-State supply, and on it section 9(1) of the Central Goods and Services Tax Act levies the central tax and the State Goods and Services Tax Act of that State (the Union Territory Goods and Services Tax Act, in a Union territory without a legislature) levies the State or Union territory tax, each at half the rate — the Central Tax (Rate) notification and each State''s own notification print the same schedules at half the integrated rate. One code carries the whole rate and its postings split it: half to the central tax account and to the Central Tax column of the line, half to the State/UT tax account and to the State/UT Tax column. `applies_when.supply_vs_seller: same` is section 8 in the vocabulary of the core: the place of supply lies in the State the seller is registered in, which is the State of its GSTIN, so the company''s own territory has to be set to that State. The rate: Schedule VII of Notification No. 9/2025-Integrated Tax (Rate), 17 September 2025, which kept 28 % for pan masala and tobacco products only (the 2017 notification had it as Schedule IV and reached far more goods). The Government moved those goods to 40 % and ended the compensation cess on them from 1 February 2026, when an additional excise duty and a Health and National Security Cess took the cess''s place, so this code closes on 31 January 2026. The taxable value goes to column 2 of line 3.1(a) of FORM GSTR-3B and the two halves of the tax to its columns 4 and 5.', 'S', null, 70, 'gst', true, '{}'::tax_condition[], null, false, false, null, 'igst-rate-9-2025', null, null, null, 'same'),
  ('IN', 'IN-S-3-INTER', 'Sale to another State — IGST 3 %', '{}'::jsonb, 'Seller and place of supply in different States: integrated tax, one posting', 'percent', 3, 'sale', 'domestic', date '2017-07-01', null, 'Section 7 of the Integrated Goods and Services Tax Act: a supply where the location of the supplier and the place of supply are in two different States, two Union territories or a State and a Union territory is an inter-State supply, and section 5(1) of the same Act levies the integrated tax on it at the whole rate, collected by the Centre alone. `applies_when.supply_vs_seller: other` is section 7 in the vocabulary of the core: the place of supply lies outside the State of the seller''s registration. The rate: Schedule IV of Notification No. 9/2025-Integrated Tax (Rate), 17 September 2025 — gold, silver, platinum and articles of jewellery; the rate stood at 3 % under Schedule V of Notification No. 1/2017 as well. The taxable value goes to column 2 of line 3.1(a) of FORM GSTR-3B and the tax to its column 3.', 'S', null, 120, 'gst', true, '{}'::tax_condition[], null, false, false, null, 'igst-rate-9-2025', null, null, null, 'other'),
  ('IN', 'IN-S-3-INTRA', 'Sale within the State — GST 3 % (CGST 1.5 % + SGST/UTGST 1.5 %)', '{}'::jsonb, 'Seller and place of supply in the same State: central tax and State tax, half each', 'percent', 3, 'sale', 'domestic', date '2017-07-01', null, 'Section 8 of the Integrated Goods and Services Tax Act: a supply where the location of the supplier and the place of supply are in the same State or the same Union territory is an intra-State supply, and on it section 9(1) of the Central Goods and Services Tax Act levies the central tax and the State Goods and Services Tax Act of that State (the Union Territory Goods and Services Tax Act, in a Union territory without a legislature) levies the State or Union territory tax, each at half the rate — the Central Tax (Rate) notification and each State''s own notification print the same schedules at half the integrated rate. One code carries the whole rate and its postings split it: half to the central tax account and to the Central Tax column of the line, half to the State/UT tax account and to the State/UT Tax column. `applies_when.supply_vs_seller: same` is section 8 in the vocabulary of the core: the place of supply lies in the State the seller is registered in, which is the State of its GSTIN, so the company''s own territory has to be set to that State. The rate: Schedule IV of Notification No. 9/2025-Integrated Tax (Rate), 17 September 2025 — gold, silver, platinum and articles of jewellery; the rate stood at 3 % under Schedule V of Notification No. 1/2017 as well. The taxable value goes to column 2 of line 3.1(a) of FORM GSTR-3B and the two halves of the tax to its columns 4 and 5.', 'S', null, 110, 'gst', true, '{}'::tax_condition[], null, false, false, null, 'igst-rate-9-2025', null, null, null, 'same'),
  ('IN', 'IN-S-40-INTER', 'Sale to another State — IGST 40 %', '{}'::jsonb, 'Seller and place of supply in different States: integrated tax, one posting', 'percent', 40, 'sale', 'domestic', date '2025-09-22', null, 'Section 7 of the Integrated Goods and Services Tax Act: a supply where the location of the supplier and the place of supply are in two different States, two Union territories or a State and a Union territory is an inter-State supply, and section 5(1) of the same Act levies the integrated tax on it at the whole rate, collected by the Centre alone. `applies_when.supply_vs_seller: other` is section 7 in the vocabulary of the core: the place of supply lies outside the State of the seller''s registration. The rate: Schedule III of Notification No. 9/2025-Integrated Tax (Rate) and of the Central Tax (Rate) notification of the same number, 17 September 2025, in force from 22 September 2025 — the rate the notification sets for the goods it lists there (aerated and caffeinated beverages, motor cars above the thresholds it prints, and from 1 February 2026 pan masala, cigarettes and manufactured tobacco other than biris). Sub-section (1) of section 5 of the Integrated Goods and Services Tax Act caps the integrated tax at forty per cent and sub-section (1) of section 9 of the Central Goods and Services Tax Act caps the central tax at twenty, which is this rate split in two. The taxable value goes to column 2 of line 3.1(a) of FORM GSTR-3B and the tax to its column 3.', 'S', null, 100, 'gst', true, '{}'::tax_condition[], null, false, false, null, 'igst-rate-9-2025', null, null, null, 'other'),
  ('IN', 'IN-S-40-INTRA', 'Sale within the State — GST 40 % (CGST 20 % + SGST/UTGST 20 %)', '{}'::jsonb, 'Seller and place of supply in the same State: central tax and State tax, half each', 'percent', 40, 'sale', 'domestic', date '2025-09-22', null, 'Section 8 of the Integrated Goods and Services Tax Act: a supply where the location of the supplier and the place of supply are in the same State or the same Union territory is an intra-State supply, and on it section 9(1) of the Central Goods and Services Tax Act levies the central tax and the State Goods and Services Tax Act of that State (the Union Territory Goods and Services Tax Act, in a Union territory without a legislature) levies the State or Union territory tax, each at half the rate — the Central Tax (Rate) notification and each State''s own notification print the same schedules at half the integrated rate. One code carries the whole rate and its postings split it: half to the central tax account and to the Central Tax column of the line, half to the State/UT tax account and to the State/UT Tax column. `applies_when.supply_vs_seller: same` is section 8 in the vocabulary of the core: the place of supply lies in the State the seller is registered in, which is the State of its GSTIN, so the company''s own territory has to be set to that State. The rate: Schedule III of Notification No. 9/2025-Integrated Tax (Rate) and of the Central Tax (Rate) notification of the same number, 17 September 2025, in force from 22 September 2025 — the rate the notification sets for the goods it lists there (aerated and caffeinated beverages, motor cars above the thresholds it prints, and from 1 February 2026 pan masala, cigarettes and manufactured tobacco other than biris). Sub-section (1) of section 5 of the Integrated Goods and Services Tax Act caps the integrated tax at forty per cent and sub-section (1) of section 9 of the Central Goods and Services Tax Act caps the central tax at twenty, which is this rate split in two. The taxable value goes to column 2 of line 3.1(a) of FORM GSTR-3B and the two halves of the tax to its columns 4 and 5.', 'S', null, 90, 'gst', true, '{}'::tax_condition[], null, false, false, null, 'igst-rate-9-2025', null, null, null, 'same'),
  ('IN', 'IN-S-5-INTER', 'Sale to another State — IGST 5 %', '{}'::jsonb, 'Seller and place of supply in different States: integrated tax, one posting', 'percent', 5, 'sale', 'domestic', date '2017-07-01', null, 'Section 7 of the Integrated Goods and Services Tax Act: a supply where the location of the supplier and the place of supply are in two different States, two Union territories or a State and a Union territory is an inter-State supply, and section 5(1) of the same Act levies the integrated tax on it at the whole rate, collected by the Centre alone. `applies_when.supply_vs_seller: other` is section 7 in the vocabulary of the core: the place of supply lies outside the State of the seller''s registration. The rate: Schedule I of Notification No. 9/2025-Integrated Tax (Rate) and of the Central Tax (Rate) notification of the same number, both of 17 September 2025 and in force from 22 September 2025, which superseded Notification No. 1/2017 of 28 June 2017; the rate stood at 5 % under the 2017 notification as well. Services at the same rate are those of Notification No. 11/2017-Central Tax (Rate), as amended with effect from the same day. The taxable value goes to column 2 of line 3.1(a) of FORM GSTR-3B and the tax to its column 3.', 'S', null, 20, 'gst', true, '{}'::tax_condition[], null, false, false, null, 'igst-rate-9-2025', null, null, null, 'other'),
  ('IN', 'IN-S-5-INTRA', 'Sale within the State — GST 5 % (CGST 2.5 % + SGST/UTGST 2.5 %)', '{}'::jsonb, 'Seller and place of supply in the same State: central tax and State tax, half each', 'percent', 5, 'sale', 'domestic', date '2017-07-01', null, 'Section 8 of the Integrated Goods and Services Tax Act: a supply where the location of the supplier and the place of supply are in the same State or the same Union territory is an intra-State supply, and on it section 9(1) of the Central Goods and Services Tax Act levies the central tax and the State Goods and Services Tax Act of that State (the Union Territory Goods and Services Tax Act, in a Union territory without a legislature) levies the State or Union territory tax, each at half the rate — the Central Tax (Rate) notification and each State''s own notification print the same schedules at half the integrated rate. One code carries the whole rate and its postings split it: half to the central tax account and to the Central Tax column of the line, half to the State/UT tax account and to the State/UT Tax column. `applies_when.supply_vs_seller: same` is section 8 in the vocabulary of the core: the place of supply lies in the State the seller is registered in, which is the State of its GSTIN, so the company''s own territory has to be set to that State. The rate: Schedule I of Notification No. 9/2025-Integrated Tax (Rate) and of the Central Tax (Rate) notification of the same number, both of 17 September 2025 and in force from 22 September 2025, which superseded Notification No. 1/2017 of 28 June 2017; the rate stood at 5 % under the 2017 notification as well. Services at the same rate are those of Notification No. 11/2017-Central Tax (Rate), as amended with effect from the same day. The taxable value goes to column 2 of line 3.1(a) of FORM GSTR-3B and the two halves of the tax to its columns 4 and 5.', 'S', null, 10, 'gst', true, '{}'::tax_condition[], null, false, false, null, 'igst-rate-9-2025', null, null, null, 'same'),
  ('IN', 'IN-S-EXEMPT', 'Exempt supply', '{}'::jsonb, 'A supply a notification under section 11 exempts from the whole of the tax', 'percent', 0, 'sale', 'exempt', date '2017-07-01', null, 'Section 11(1) of the Central Goods and Services Tax Act lets the Government, on the recommendations of the Council, exempt goods or services of any specified description from the whole of the tax; the exemptions are those of Notification No. 2/2017-Central Tax (Rate) for goods and No. 12/2017-Central Tax (Rate) for services, and their integrated tax twins — among the services, the renting of a residential dwelling for use as a residence to a person who is not registered, and a loan or deposit whose consideration is interest. Section 17(2) and rule 42 of the Central Goods and Services Tax Rules take back the credit attributable to it. The value goes to column 2 of line 3.1(c) of FORM GSTR-3B.', 'E', null, 290, 'gst', true, array['supply_nature']::tax_condition[], null, false, false, null, 'cgst-s11', null, null, null, null),
  ('IN', 'IN-S-NIL', 'Nil-rated supply', '{}'::jsonb, 'Goods or services the rate notifications tax at zero', 'percent', 0, 'sale', 'domestic', date '2017-07-01', null, 'A supply of goods or services the rate notifications tax at nil, reported with the exempted supplies in column 2 of line 3.1(c) of FORM GSTR-3B, “Other outward supplies (Nil rated, exempted)”. Unlike a zero-rated supply under section 16 of the Integrated Goods and Services Tax Act, it gives no right to a refund of the credit behind it, and rule 42 of the Central Goods and Services Tax Rules reverses the common credit attributable to it.', 'Z', null, 280, 'gst', true, array['supply_nature']::tax_condition[], null, false, false, null, 'gstr-3b-form', null, null, null, null),
  ('IN', 'IN-S-NONGST', 'Non-GST supply', '{}'::jsonb, 'Alcoholic liquor for human consumption and the five petroleum products not yet under GST', 'percent', 0, 'sale', 'not_subject', date '2017-07-01', null, 'Section 9(1) of the Central Goods and Services Tax Act levies the tax on all intra-State supplies except the supply of alcoholic liquor for human consumption, and section 9(2) defers the tax on petroleum crude, high speed diesel, motor spirit, natural gas and aviation turbine fuel to a date the Government has not notified; section 5(1) and (2) of the Integrated Goods and Services Tax Act say the same of inter-State supplies. Those supplies are outside the tax, and FORM GSTR-3B reports their value on its own line, 3.1(e), “Non-GST outward supplies”.', 'O', null, 300, 'gst', true, array['supply_nature']::tax_condition[], null, false, false, null, 'cgst-s9', null, null, null, null),
  ('IN', 'IN-S-ZR-LUT', 'Zero-rated supply — export or supply to an SEZ, under bond or Letter of Undertaking', '{}'::jsonb, 'No integrated tax charged; the credit behind it stays available and its refund is claimed', 'percent', 0, 'sale', 'export', date '2017-07-01', null, 'Section 16(1) of the Integrated Goods and Services Tax Act: a zero rated supply is an export of goods or services, or a supply for authorised operations to a Special Economic Zone developer or unit. Section 16(2) keeps the input tax credit available for making it, notwithstanding that the supply may be exempt, and section 16(3) lets the supplier make it without payment of integrated tax under bond or Letter of Undertaking and claim refund of the unutilised credit under section 54 of the Central Goods and Services Tax Act — which is what this code is. Section 7(5) makes such a supply inter-State whatever the States involved, so no State tax arises. Rule 46 of the Central Goods and Services Tax Rules requires the invoice to carry the endorsement “SUPPLY MEANT FOR EXPORT/SUPPLY TO SEZ UNIT OR SEZ DEVELOPER FOR AUTHORISED OPERATIONS UNDER BOND OR LETTER OF UNDERTAKING WITHOUT PAYMENT OF INTEGRATED TAX”, and the value goes to column 2 of line 3.1(b) of FORM GSTR-3B. The other route of section 16(3), export on payment of integrated tax with a refund of the tax paid, is not carried by this pack: the README says why.', 'G', null, 270, 'gst', true, array['transport_evidence', 'buyer_status']::tax_condition[], null, false, false, null, 'igst-s16', null, null, null, null)
